      'Rule example: Build all four foundations from Ace to King in suit. The game is won when all 52 cards are on the foundations.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Turn a card from the stock onto the waste; only the topmost card of the waste may be played. 2. The top waste card may be moved to a foundation (build up in suit from Ace to King) or to a tableau pile. 3. On the tableau, build down in alternating colors; any card may be placed on an empty tableau pile. 4. You may move one or more cards from one tableau pile to another when the build rule holds. 5. Only one pass through the stock is allowed; there is no redeal.',
      'Scoring example: Points or match rules. Win when all four foundations are built from Ace to King in suit (all 52 cards on foundations)..',
